---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Sounds So Far"
  description="How Sounds So Far handles the information you share with us."
  noindex
>
<main>
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
    <p class="legal-notice">This is a plain-language draft and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Don't treat it as final.</p>

    <p class="lead">This page covers what happens to the information you give us through this site — the artist application, the contact form, and the newsletter sign-up.</p>

    <h3>What we collect</h3>
    <p class="lead">When you fill out a form on this site, we collect what you type into it — things like your name, email, phone number, hometown, and anything else the form asks for. If you upload a recording, we store that file too.</p>

    <h3>What we use it for</h3>
    <p class="lead">To review artist applications, to reply to messages sent through the contact form, and to send newsletter emails to people who sign up for them. We don't sell your information to anyone.</p>

    <h3>Where it's stored</h3>
    <p class="lead">Form submissions are stored and processed by Netlify Forms. Newsletter sign-ups will be stored by whichever email service we end up using (not yet chosen as of this writing).</p>

    <h3>Recordings and live sets</h3>
    <p class="lead">If you're invited to play, your set and podcast interview may be recorded and posted publicly, as described on the artist application. You keep ownership of your music.</p>

    <h3>Unsubscribing</h3>
    <p class="lead">Every newsletter email will include a way to unsubscribe. You can also email us directly to ask that your information be removed.</p>

    <h3>Questions</h3>
    <p class="lead">Reach out through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
</Layout>
